# Settings for baking art (anim's export, `plugins/anim/anim.export.py`, and the bake scripts in
# games' assets/). Copy this file to `.env` beside it and set what differs on your machine; `.env` is
# not committed. A variable already set in the shell wins over `.env`. Playing a game reads neither.

# Blender's binary, an absolute path. Unset, it is the macOS application's:
# BLENDER=/Applications/Blender.app/Contents/MacOS/Blender

# The library the bakes read raw parts from: a rigged character is `characters/<name>/<name>.fbx`
# in it. `~` is your home folder. Unset, it is:
# PATCHWORK_LIBRARY=~/patchwork-library

# gltfpack, the native build (1.3 or later, from https://github.com/zeux/meshoptimizer/releases), which
# packs WebP textures; the npm build in node_modules is the node.js one and cannot. Unset, it is
# `gltfpack` on the PATH:
# GLTFPACK=/usr/local/bin/gltfpack

# ImageMagick's `magick`, built with libwebp, which writes the loose textures as WebP. Unset, it is
# `magick` on the PATH:
# MAGICK=/opt/homebrew/bin/magick

# `yarn health` checks every one of these.
